sers/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"status":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"parent_issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/1184","issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Part of epic #1184 (PM stack coherence — ideal-system design series, 2026-10-26).\n\n## Why\nThe stack's own reliability is currently vibes: pages degrade silently, the watchdog concept (#1148) alerts after the fact, and common failures (collector stopped, feed not pushed, a facet down) wait for a human or an hourly job. The ideal stack declares per-facet freshness SLOs with error budgets on the health page, and the watchdog remediates the known failure classes itself — restart the collector, re-push the feed, re-render config — escalating to Drew only when remediation fails or budget burns.\n\n## Design questions to answer\n- SLO definitions per facet (feed age, quota read age, orchestration freshness, per-service up): targets, windows, and how budget remaining is computed and displayed.\n- Remediation catalogue: which failures are auto-fixable (collector restart, feed re-push, aggregator restart, tunnel restart), with what guardrails, attempt caps, and cooldowns?\n- Verification after remediation: how does the watchdog prove the fix worked before standing down, and where is the attempt logged?\n- Escalation: what pages Drew (via the PWA/push design) vs lands in NEEDS ORCHESTRATOR, and how does a burning error budget change that threshold?\n- Safety: what the watchdog must never do (data writes, deploys, credential changes) and how its own failure is detected.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Design note landed in repo `doc/` + implementation issues filed and linked as sub-issues of #1184; open questions needing Drew named explicitly in the design note.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A design note answering every question listed under \"Design questions to answer\" is landed in the repo `doc/` tree and linked from this issue.\n- Implementation issues are filed and linked as sub-issues of epic #1184 (developing-today/code), each with its own acceptance criteria — this design issue does not itself carry implementation work.\n- Every open question that needs Drew is named explicitly in the design note (not buried in prose).\n- The remediation catalogue carries per-action guardrails, attempt caps, and cooldowns, and the design names what the watchdog must never do (data writes, deploys, credential changes).\n","closed_by":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5